  <subsection title="Determine Whether a Fraction is a Solution of an Equation">
    <p>As we saw in Solve Equations with the Subtraction and Addition Properties of Equality and Solve Equations Using Integers; The Division Property of Equality, a solution of an equation is a value that makes a true statement when substituted for the variable in the equation. In those sections, we found whole number and integer solutions to equations. Now that we have worked with fractions, we are ready to find fraction solutions to equations.</p>
    <p>The steps we take to determine whether a number is a solution to an equation are the same whether the solution is a whole number, an integer, or a fraction.</p>
    <note type="How To">
      <list type="ol" style="1">
        <item>Step 1. 
Substitute the number for the variable in the equation.</item>
        <item>Step 2. 
Simplify the expressions on both sides of the equation.</item>
        <item>Step 3. 
Determine whether the resulting equation is true. If it is true, the number is a solution. If it is not true, the number is not a solution.</item>
      </list>
    </note>
    <example number="4.95">
      <problem>
        <p>Determine whether each of the following is a solution of $$x - \frac{3}{10} = \frac{1}{2}.$$</p>
        <list type="ol" style="1">
