          <item>ⓑ $$x = \frac{4}{5}$$</item>
          <item>ⓒ $$x = - \frac{4}{5}$$</item>
        </list>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <table>
          <tbody>
            <row>
              <cell>ⓐ</cell>
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell />
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell />
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Change to fractions with a LCD of 10.</cell>
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Subtract.</cell>
              <cell />
            </row>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p>Since $$x = 1$$ does not result in a true equation, $$1$$ is not a solution to the equation.</p>
        <table>
          <tbody>
            <row>
              <cell>ⓑ</cell>
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell />
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell />
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell />
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Subtract.</cell>
              <cell />
            </row>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p>Since $$x = \frac{4}{5}$$ results in a true equation, $$\frac{4}{5}$$ is a solution to the equation $$x - \frac{3}{10} = \frac{1}{2}.$$</p>
        <table>
          <tbody>
            <row>
              <cell>ⓒ</cell>
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell />
