  <subsection title="Solve Equations with Fractions Using the Multiplication Property of Equality">
    <p>Consider the equation $$4$$ We want to know what number divided by $$3.$$ gives $$4.$$ So to “undo” the division, we will need to multiply by $$a,b,$$ The Multiplication Property of Equality will allow us to do this. This property says that if we start with two equal quantities and multiply both by the same number, the results are equal.</p>
    <note type="The Multiplication Property of Equality">
      <p>For any numbers $$c,$$ and $$\text{if}\ a = b,\text{then}\ ac = bc.$$</p>
      <equation>$$\frac{x}{7} = -9.$$</equation>
      <p>If you multiply both sides of an equation by the same quantity, you still have equality.</p>
    </note>
    <p>Let’s use the Multiplication Property of Equality to solve the equation $$\frac{x}{7} = -9.$$</p>
    <example number="4.99">
      <problem>
        <p>Solve: $$7$$</p>
