  <subsection title="Translate Sentences to Equations and Solve">
    <p>Now we have covered all four properties of equality—subtraction, addition, division, and multiplication. We’ll list them all together here for easy reference.</p>
    <table>
      <tbody>
        <row>
          <cell>Subtraction Property of Equality:For any real numbers $$\textit{c,}$$ and $$a = b,$$if $$a - c = b - c.$$ then $$\textit{a, b,}$$</cell>
          <cell>Addition Property of Equality:For any real numbers $$\textit{c,}$$ and $$a = b,$$if $$a + c = b + c.$$ then $$\textit{a, b,}$$</cell>
        </row>
        <row>
          <cell>Division Property of Equality:For any numbers $$\textit{c,}$$ and $$\textit{c} \neq 0$$ where $$a = b,$$if $$\frac{a}{c} = \frac{b}{c}$$ then $$\textit{a, b,}$$</cell>
          <cell>Multiplication Property of Equality:For any real numbers $$\textit{c}$$ and $$a = b,$$if $$ac = bc$$ then $$n$$</cell>
        </row>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>When you add, subtract, multiply or divide the same quantity from both sides of an equation, you still have equality.</p>
    <p>In the next few examples, we’ll translate sentences into equations and then solve the equations. It might be helpful to review the translation table in Evaluate, Simplify, and Translate Expressions.</p>
