    <example number="4.107">
      <problem>
        <p>Translate and solve: The quotient of $$\frac{5}{6}$$ and $$\frac{3}{4}.$$ is $$m$$</p>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <table summary="This table demonstrates the step-by-step process of solving and verifying an algebraic equation involving fractions for the variable 'm'.">
          <tbody>
            <row>
              <cell />
              <cell>The quotient of $$\frac{5}{6}$$ and $$\frac{3}{4}$$ is $$\frac{\ m\ }{\frac{5}{6}} = \frac{3}{4}$$.</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Translate.</cell>
              <cell>$$\frac{5}{6}$$</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Multiply both sides by $$m$$ to isolate $$\frac{5}{6}\left( \frac{\ m\ }{\frac{5}{6}} \right) = \frac{5}{6}\left( \frac{3}{4} \right)$$.</cell>
              <cell>$$m = \frac{5 \cdot 3}{6 \cdot 4}$$</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Simplify.</cell>
              <cell>$$m = \frac{5}{8}$$</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Remove common factors and multiply.</cell>
              <cell>$$\frac{5}{8}$$</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Check:</cell>
              <cell />
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Is the quotient of $$\frac{5}{6}$$ and $$\frac{3}{4}$$ equal to $$\frac{\ \frac{5}{8}\ }{\ \frac{5}{6}\ }\overset{?}{=}\frac{3}{4}$$?</cell>
              <cell>$$\frac{5}{8} \div \frac{5}{6}\overset{?}{=}\frac{3}{4}$$</cell>
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Rewrite as division.</cell>
              <cell>$$\frac{5}{8} \cdot \frac{6}{5}\overset{?}{=}\frac{3}{4}$$</cell>
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Multiply the first fraction by the reciprocal of the second.</cell>
              <cell>$$\frac{3}{4} = \frac{3}{4}✓$$</cell>
              <cell />
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Simplify.</cell>
              <cell>$$n$$</cell>
              <cell />
            </row>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p>Our solution checks.</p>
      </solution>
    </example>
